  "text": "### 3. Capital Adequacy & Stress Testing  \n**Summary:**\nCFO presented capital position and 2026 stress testing scenarios.  \n**Current Capital Position:**\n- Capital Ratio: 18.2% (Pillar 1: 15% minimum)\n- Capital Buffer: 3.2% above minimum\n- Assessment: **Comfortable position**, no capital raising needed 2026  \n**Stress Testing Scenarios (2026 Plan):**\n1. **Recession Scenario:** 2% economic contraction\n- Expected capital impact: -2.1% (ratio falls to 16.1%)\n- Assessment: **Resilient**, still above minimum  \n2. **Fraud Shock:** £250k fraud incident\n- Expected capital impact: -0.3% (ratio falls to 17.9%)\n- Assessment: **Manageable**, standard reserves sufficient  \n3. **Operational Loss:** Major system outage, customer losses\n- Expected capital impact: -0.8% (ratio falls to 17.4%)\n- Assessment: **Absorbed**, recovery plan documented  \n**Committee Decision:**\n✅ **APPROVED** 2026 stress testing plan.  \n**Action Items:**\n- CFO to conduct stress tests by end of Q2 2026\n- Report findings to committee in June 2026 meeting  \n---",
